    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released **version 2 of the owner identity** across four areas, mixing a fixed `\"V2\"` version tag into every identifier so each one changes and no v1 value is reproduced \u2014 while keeping the user-facing `locality`/`timezone`/segment region as the plain region code.\n\n**Identity derivation (v2 tag mixed in):**\n- `Owner.identityKey(...)` (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 now hashes `\"V2\" | telephone | email | soundex(lastName)`; added the public `IDENTITY_VERSION = \"V2\"` constant. Still a 64-hex SHA-256.\n- `assignMemberId(...)` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 the region code inside the memberId is now `\"V2\" + regionFor(...)` (e.g. `V2NSW27786E13D53`).\n- `householdIdFor(...)` \u2014 now hashes `\"V2\" | collapse(lastName) | postcode`; still identical for owners sharing lastName+postcode.\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`):**\n- Removed top-level `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`.\n- Added a nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema) holding those three, built via a static `identityOf(owner)` helper.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- `locality` (plain `NSW`), `timezone`, and `ownerSegment` (rule unchanged, plain region) all preserved.\n\n**Audit event (`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`):**\n- Moved to schema version 2 with an added `\"schemaVersion\":2`, still carrying `ownerId` and the v2 `memberId`.\n\n**Request fields:** unchanged.\n\nVerification: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 70, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the v2 checkpoints (Cp60 apiVersion/grouping, Cp53 audit schemaVersion, Cp56/Cp32/Cp52/Cp28/Cp36/Cp11/Cp41/Cp57) and the unchanged-behaviour ones (Cp17 locality `NSW`, Cp42 timezone, Cp55 segment `STANDARD_METRO`).",
