    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The mapping lives on the generated `OwnersApi` interface (`POST /owners`), implemented by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` under the class-level `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")`.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. *(Only actually enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; with security disabled the annotation is not wired up.)*\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 declarative constraints from the OpenAPI-generated DTO:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters + up to two spaced/hyphenated/apostrophed parts), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 valid `LocalDate`, nullable\n   \n   Failure \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\n## Inside the controller body (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before and that owner still exists, return it with **200 OK** (no new owner created). *(This is the only branch that skips everything below.)*\n4. `normalizeAddress` *(side-effect)* \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST/RD/AVE, and composes the persisted `address`.\n5. `validateRequiredFields` *(validation)* \u2014 `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else **400** (`RequiredFieldsMissingException`).\n6. `validatePostcode` *(validation)* \u2014 if a postcode is present, it must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`).\n7. `normalizeTelephone` *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 converts to E.164, enforcing country-specific digit counts (+61\u21929, +1\u219210); invalid \u2192 **400**.\n8. `normalizeEmail` *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 if email present: must match the email pattern, must not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail); stored lower-cased \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidEmailException`).\n9. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` *(validation)* \u2014 computes a SHA-256 identity key over `telephone | lower(email) | soundex(lastName)`; if any non-deleted owner shares it \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n10. `rejectCityAtCapacity` *(validation)* \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n11. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` *(validation)* \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n12. `defaultRegistrationDate` *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults to today if absent, then rolls forward off weekends/public holidays to the next business day.\n13. `rejectDailyLimit` *(validation)* \u2014 \u2265 100 owners already registered on that business day \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`).\n\n## Building the entity (side-effects \u2014 derived field assignment)\n\n14. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` \u2014 MapStruct maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`id` and `pets` ignored).\n15. Derived fields assigned, in this order (each scans all owners via `findAllOwners()`):\n    - `assignMemberId` (SHA-256 + Luhn, region/FY-coded, collision de-dup)\n    - `assignHouseholdId`\n    - `assignHouseholdMemberCount`\n    - `assignMembershipLevelCap` (honors `sharesHousehold` flag)\n    - `assignNamesakeCount`\n    - `assignBulkSignupWarning` (>80 that day)\n    - `assignCapacityWarning` (40\u201349 in city)\n    - `assignPossibleDuplicate` (soundex + postcode soft match, honors `sharesHousehold`)\n\n## Persist and post-persist side-effects\n\n16. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 the single DB write, `@Transactional`, via `ownerRepository.save` (identity-column ID generated).\n17. **Record idempotency mapping** \u2014 stores `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner.id`.\n18. **`AUDIT.info(...)`** \u2014 human-readable audit log line.\n19. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON to the audit log with an incrementing sequence number (schema version 2).\n20. **`NOTIFY.info(...)`** \u2014 \"welcome owner\" notification log line.\n21. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` \u2014 computes all derived read-only response fields.\n22. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and returns **201 Created**.\n\n## Two nuances worth flagging\n\n- The entity-level constraints on `Owner`/`Person` (`@NotEmpty` on `firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone`, `@Pattern` E.164 on `telephone`) are **not** enforced on this path \u2014 validation happens on the DTO and via the manual helper methods; the entity is never re-validated with `@Valid` before `save`. There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.) or Spring `ApplicationEvent`s \u2014 the \"events\" above are log output.\n- `sharesHousehold` is a write-only control flag: it influences steps 15 (`assignMembershipLevelCap`, `assignPossibleDuplicate`) but is never persisted or returned."
